    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4, Chap 396 of 2012",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8675\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 396 of the laws of 2012 amending the education\nlaw relating to services to out-of-state school districts by boards of\ncooperative educational services, in relation to the effectiveness ther-\neof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo extend authorization for BOCES to lease with private entities for 20\nyears till July 1, 2029.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends 396 of the laws of 2012 amending the education law to\nextend the effective date to July 1, 2029.\n\nSection 2 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nBoards of cooperative educational services (BOCES) are often at the\nforefront of innovative and cost-saving educational plans, policies, and\nprograms. BOCES, as innovators in the development and delivery of highly\nsuccessful curricula, professional development for educators and proven\neducation programs, are already providing these programs and services to\nschools in New York State. Prior to enactment of Chapter 396 of the Laws\nof 2012, BOCES was not authorized to enter into contracts with out-of-\nstate schools. Since this law was enacted, several BOCES have, and\ncontinue to, provide these services to schools located outside of New\nYork.\n\nThis authorization is scheduled to expire on July 1, 2024. This bill\nwould extend it for a further 5 years, until July 1, 2029.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
